  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the relationship between $p$ and $q$:**\n   Since $p$ and $q$ are inversely proportional, we have:\n   \\[\n   pq = k\n   \\]\n   where $k$ is a constant.\n\n2. **Find the constant $k$:**\n   Given $p=25$ and $q=6$, we substitute these values into the equation:\n   \\[\n   25 \\times 6 = k\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   k = 150\n   \\]\n\n3. **Use the constant $k$ to find $p$ when $q=15$:**\n   Given $q=15$, we substitute into the equation $pq = 150$:\n   \\[\n   p \\times 15 = 150\n   \\]\n   Solving for $p$, we get:\n   \\[\n   p = \\frac{150}{15}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   p = 10\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   The value of $p$ when $q=15$ is $\\boxed{10}$.",
